bels/accepted","name":"accepted","color":"0052cc","default":false,"description":"There is consensus among the team that this change meets the criteria for inclusion"},{"id":829215248,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4MjkyMTUyNDg=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/labels/archived%20due%20to%20age","name":"archived due to age","color":"eeeeee","default":false,"description":"This issue has been archived; please open a new issue for any further discussion"}],"state":"closed","locked":true,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2015-08-19T20:53:14Z","updated_at":"2018-02-07T00:39:48Z","closed_at":"2015-08-20T16:24:59Z","author_association":"MEMBER","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Problem description\n\nIn my `.eslintrc` I’ve configured the `one-var` rule as `\"one-var\": 2`, according to the [rule documentation](http://eslint.org/docs/rules/one-var#options) the default option should be `\"one-var\": [2, \"always\"]`.\n\nIf I try to lint the following code with `\"one-var\":  2`\n\n``` js\nvar foo = 'a';\nvar bar = 'b';\n```\n\nI get no error. When I set the configuration to `\"one-var\": [2, \"always\"]` in my `.eslintrc` then I get the expected errors.\n\n---\n## Reproducible in the online demo\n\nNo error:\n\n``` js\n/*eslint \"one-var\": 2 */\nvar foo = 'a';\nvar bar = 'b';\n```\n\nWorks as expected:\n\n``` js\n/*eslint \"one-var\": [2, \"always\"] */\nvar foo = 'a';\nvar bar = 'b';\n```\n\n---\n\nSeems like the default options were removed in commit e4076d2855dcc1450d51c1bbe79b7749d546f052.\n","closed_by":{"login":"nzakas","id":38546,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38546?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas","html_url":"https://github.com/nzakas","followers_url":"http